analysis:
The PR changes only docs/architecture/inference.md. It adds one paragraph at head lines 595-611 describing a four-row Gated DeltaNet prompt-window recurrence kernel for qwen3_5, qwen3_5_moe and prism_hadamard_qwen35. Kernel selection is a one-time probe per kernel instantiation. It picks packed, then rows, whichever reproduces gated_delta_step bit for bit on the GPU, and otherwise falls back to the stock kernel. Decode, MTP verification, masked updates and short windows keep the stock kernel. A new env var, DARKBLOOM_TTFT_GDN_BLOCKED, can force a kernel for A/B measurement. I examined the base text of both units (lines 1-797 of the doc) and the patch. No code, trust-boundary, auth, encryption, attestation or billing change is visible.

The doc claims bit-exact equivalence with the stock kernel. If true, it preserves recurrent-state integrity for streamed prefix-cache checkpoints (T-041 context). Since the source is not supplied here, that claim is unverified. Nothing in the supplied evidence shows a regression. The next pass should check, if the code is in the PR, GatedDelta.swift for:
- whether the probe fails closed to the stock kernel;
- whether a forced kernel can bypass the bit-exact probe (operator-only, so it is not an adversary-controlled input);
- whether any state mismatch could poison cached checkpoints across tenants.

The prefix-cache and TTFT timing-oracle posture (SEC-035) is not weakened by this documentation. A faster prefill could change TTFT characteristics but not the hit/miss structure.
